<section id="about" class="section" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
  <SectionHeading number="03" title="A little context" id="about-heading" note="Experience Architecture / Michigan State University" />
  <div class="about-grid"><p class="about-statement">Connecting information,<br />interaction, and implementation.</p><div><p>I’m a UX / Product Designer completing my B.A. in Experience Architecture at Michigan State University. I have one credit remaining, with expected graduation in December 2026.</p><p>My academic work explores how people understand information and move through tasks. In collaborative projects, I’ve participated in interviews, heuristic evaluation, task mapping, and interface prototyping—from academic workflows in D2L to event participation in Community Spaces.</p><p>My frontend background informs how I think about responsive behavior, accessibility, and the practical details of an interface. I’m interested in UX and Product Design opportunities where I can connect careful analysis with clear interaction design.</p><aside id="resume" class="resume-note" aria-labelledby="resume-heading"><h3 id="resume-heading">Resume</h3>{site.resumeHref ? <a class="text-link" href={site.resumeHref}>Read the resume (PDF) <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a> : <><p>The resume is awaiting owner approval for this review. Dates and employment details will be published only after confirmation.</p><span class="content-note">Resume pending approval</span></>}</aside><details class="site-implementation"><summary>About this site</summary><p>This portfolio uses Astro, TypeScript, semantic HTML, and CSS. Project records include evidence references; automated checks cover content provenance, keyboard navigation, responsive layouts, and accessibility.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/koncagu2-cloud/enhanced-portfolio">View the portfolio source and review history</a></p></details></div></div>
</section>
